        "execSummary":  "This piece reinforces NVIDIA\u0027s position as the de facto compute backbone for frontier AI model development — a strategic fact that enterprise AI leaders need to factor into their supply chain and vendor risk assessments. As AI models grow more complex and multimodal, the concentration of training infrastructure on a single vendor\u0027s platform creates both capability advantages and dependency risks worth monitoring. For enterprise AI strategy teams, understanding which models run on which infrastructure has implications for performance roadmaps, pricing trajectory, and geopolitical supply-chain exposure. The key implication: NVIDIA\u0027s infrastructure dominance means enterprise AI capability timelines are, in part, NVIDIA capability timelines — vendor diversification strategies should account for this dependency.",
