        "date":  "2026-09-17",
        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "Dan Roberts presents seven essential leadership capabilities for IT executives navigating AI-driven transformation: Coherence, Communication, Currency, Confidence, Conviction, Courage, and Change. These interconnected skills form a compounding leadership flywheel that helps leaders make faster decisions with incomplete information. The article draws on real CIO examples from BNY, J\u0026J, Liberty Mutual, Cox Automotive, GSK, and Cardinal Health.",
        "execSummary":  "Senior IT leaders face an accelerating decision environment where AI amplifies both opportunity and organizational disruption simultaneously. Roberts argues that technical proficiency is now table stakes, and the differentiating factor is a specific cluster of seven leadership behaviors that compound over time. For enterprise leaders in AI transformation, this framework directly informs how to structure executive development and evaluate leadership readiness. The implication: AI strategy without leadership capability investment will stall at the execution layer.",
