        "url":  "https://www.cio.com/article/4221996/how-roche-drives-ai-outcomes-in-a-changing-world.html",
        "date":  "2026-09-16",
        "theme":  "Enterprise",
        "summary":  "Roche CDTO Wafaa Mamilli explains how the pharmaceutical company uses AI and trusted data across drug discovery, diagnostics, manufacturing, and patient care. She emphasizes that AI success depends on governance, employee upskilling, and process reimagination rather than technical expertise alone. The conversation illustrates how a global enterprise operationalizes AI at scale with a focus on outcomes over tooling.",
        "execSummary":  "Roche\u0027s AI transformation story is notable because it centers governance and talent over technology procurement — a direct counter to the common enterprise pattern of platform-first adoption. Mamilli\u0027s framework insists that data trust is a prerequisite to AI value, not a follow-on concern. For enterprise AI strategy leaders, the Roche model is a credible reference architecture for scaling AI responsibly in regulated, high-stakes environments. The implication: organizations that skip the governance and upskilling foundation will accumulate AI debt that compounds as deployments scale.",
